==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sweet Bro Cats''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gelato Bro Cats''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Their immunity to [[Wave Attack|waves]] and Long Distance slow makes them very useful against enemies such as [[Kory]] and [[Dober P.D]]. A stack of Lifeguard Cats can consistently slow down [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies thanks to their decent uptime and slow chance. However, this slow will seldom be used because they are outranged so often.

Their DPS is not bad either, on the same level as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]]'s, letting them be a good general attacker. However, their movement speed is leagues slower than Vaulter Cat's, and their range is no better.

Once unlocked, though, [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] entirely outclasses them, as Hitman has a much lower recharge time, higher health, more than double their base damage, and has immunities to both Waves AND Freeze. Not even their True Form can save them from being outclassed, as even their 20,400 damage against Behemoths is nearly matched by Hitman's 18,700 damage, and that's not even counting Hitman's massive damage against Traitless. To add insult to injury, Hitman Cat is usable in {{4c}} while Lifeguard Cats are stuck as a Super Rare.

==='''True Form'''===
Gelato Bro Cats gain Behemoth Slayer, thus increasing their already respectable Long Distance DPS against Behemoth enemies to almost 4.3k at level 30. While their survivability is not the best, it also improves against Behemoth enemies, especially [[Cumulus Gallus]] (though it requires exactly level 31 to survive a hit). However, this improvement to survivability is still slight and dependent on luck.

